{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpm7EVhpq9aPsqaT2aAK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The assertion fails with a timeout error. `expect.poll` doesn't wait forever for your callback. It enforces the overall `timeout` (5 seconds by default in Playwright, 1 second in Vitest). If the callback's promise is still pending when that runs out, the poll stops and rejects. You get a \"timeout exceeded\" error, so the test fails the same way it would if the value never matched. No further calls are made, so it never gets to try another `intervals` attempt.\n\nTwo practical points:\n- You must `await` the `expect.poll(...)` call. If you don't, the test can finish before the rejection is reported.\n- If the callback can hang, such as a network call with no timeout of its own, give it its own shorter timeout. Otherwise one stuck call uses up the whole polling window.\n\nI answered this from memory and didn't check the current Playwright or Vitest docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2448,"cache_read_input_tokens":1693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2448},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da1058c3-683c-4c62-b904-8f3316cbd6c0","uuid":"6349ce24-8d24-4a28-b612-d3546ee68a29","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:21:54.144Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpm7EG4M5cuEksCVZmzX"}
